From a6e6ae197642be82c9ac42b1348969806f8de4fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:36:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin F-223A: experimental screen-space lamp light pass on
 Vulkan (hdLightPass, default off)

- Every M2 point light of the frame (HD::LightsGather, the D3D9 HD lamps' gathering) is culled to the view and the
  nearest hdLightPassMax uploaded; one compute stage at AfterOpaqueWorld builds per-tile lamp lists from depth and
  lights each pixel with WoW Forever's lamp falloff, applied as colour x (1 + lamp / engine light)^(1/2.2) with the
  engine light estimated from the sun's ambient+diffuse. No G-buffer: works under MSAA; no 4-light cap.
- Replace, not add: while the pass runs, CM2Lighting::AddLight drops point lights (models, terrain, WMO groups), so
  nothing is lit twice; fail-safe back to stock lamps if the stage did not fire. hdLightPassStock keeps stock lamps.
- CVars hdLightPass, Strength, Max, Radius, Floor, Stock, Debug, Info. D3D9 and pass-off paths unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UHcJJVC4feQ4s15e9bNRoN
